data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":139,"item_id":"msg_0dd7ada7fbe6854a016af580972ed487d0b1561cef5cd9e028","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"Since \\(x\\equiv2\\pmod3\\) and \\(x\\equiv2\\pmod7\\), we have \\(x\\equiv2\\pmod{21}\\), so write \\(x=2+21k\\). The condition \\(x\\equiv3\\pmod5\\) gives \\(k\\equiv1\\pmod5\\); the smallest suitable \\(k\\) is 1, giving \\(x=23\\).\n\nCheck: \\(23\\) leaves remainders \\(2,3,2\\) upon division by \\(3,5,7\\), respectively.","logprobs":[]}

